bothNow.text:
In the midst of Eden a tree budded forth death,
and in the midst of all the world a tree hath budded forth life;
for they who were once incorrupt became corrupt upon tasting the former,
but they who have received the latter have inherited incorruption.
For, as God, Thou dost save the human race through Thy Cross.

ode4.irmos:
O Lord, I have heard the mystery of Thy dispensation;
I have considered Thy works,//
and I have glorified Thy Divinity.

ode5.irmos:
Rising early we cry to Thee, O Lord;
save us, for Thou art our God,//
and we know none other besides Thee.
